    "title": "Frozen Four 2026 Schedule: Here's What To Know - FloHockey",
    "text": "On Thursday April 9, four teams converge in two Frozen Four semifinal matchups, each compelling in its own way. North Dakota, the No. 1 seed out of the Sioux Falls Regional, meets an upstart Wisconsin Badgers team that are attending their first Frozen Four since 2010. Nodak has looked unstoppable thus far in the tournament, having not given up a goal yet, but they'll still have to make it past a Badgers program that is riding high after a comeback victory against Michigan State. NCAA Men's Frozen Four Preview With FloHockey's Called Up PodcastRead The Latest 2026 NHL Draft Coverage On FloHockeySee FloHockey's Full Schedule Of GamesOn the other side of the Frozen Four, Albany Regional No. 1 seed Michigan takes on Denver, who defeated the 2026 national champion Western Michigan en route to the NCAA semifinals. The Pios are also coming off winning a tough NCHC conference tournament. Michigan, for their part, bring scoring and star power with T.J. Hughes and Michael Hage. This year's Frozen Four and NCAA men's championship final will take place at T-Mobile Arena, the home of the Vegas Golden Knights. Here's what to know. Frozen Four 2026 ScheduleThursday, April 95:00 p.m. ET: Semifinals: North Dakota vs. Wisconsin - ESPN28:30 p.m. ET: Semifinals: Michigan vs. Denver - ESPN2Saturday, April 115:30 p.m. ET - Division I Men's National Championship Game - ESPNHow To Watch The Frozen Four 2026The 2026 NCAA Men's Frozen Four will be broadcast on ESPN2, with the final being broadcast on ESPN. The games will also stream on ESPN+.NCAA Men's Hockey Scores & BracketRegional SemifinalsThursday, March 26No. 3 Michigan State 2, UConn 1Quinnipiac 5, Providence 2Wisconsin 5, Dartmouth 1No. 2 North Dakota 3, Merrimack 0Friday, March 27No. 4 Western Michigan 3, Minnesota State 1No. 1 Michigan 5, Bentley 1Denver 5, Cornell 0Minnesota Duluth 3, Penn State 1Regional FinalsSaturday, March 28Wisconsin 4, No. 3 Michigan State 3 (OT)No. 2 North Dakota 5, Quinnipiac 0Sunday, March 29Denver 6, No. 4 Western Michigan 2No. 1 Michigan 4, Minnesota Duluth 3Frozen FourThursday, April 95:00 p.m. ET: Semifinals: North Dakota vs. Wisconsin - ESPN28:30 p.m. ET: Semifinals: Michigan vs. Denver - ESPN2Saturday, April 115:30 p.m. ET - DI Men's National Championship - ESPNWhere Is The Frozen Four 2026?The NCAA Men’s Frozen Four is coming to Las Vegas for the first time in 2026. The event will be held at T-Mobile Arena, home of the Vegas Golden Knights, on April 9.Watch the AHL, ECHL, OHL, QMJHL, USHL And More On FloHockeyFloHockey is the streaming home to some of the best hockey leagues in North America, including the ECHL and more. Check out the broadcast schedule to watch more hockey.Join The Hockey Conversation On FloHockey SocialFollow us on Twitter @FloHockeyFollow us on Instagram @flohockeyFollow us on TikTok @flohockeytvWatch us on YouTubeLike us on Facebook",
